# pyron POOL-VS-POOL CONTACT at the FATAL map index (14z-129).
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS. tests/audit_hitclass_map_cost.sh section 0 needs a
# POSITIVE CRASH CONTROL: an END-clean soak with the hit-class thunk proves
# nothing unless the SAME rig CRASHES without it. Its old control — the
# 11,017-frame pyron mash soak — stopped reaching the map at all (section 4:
# "total=0 ext=0 trap=0"), so the control was DEAD and the gate said so
# rather than give a verdict.
#
# WHAT WAS MISSING WAS CONTACT, NOT EXPOSURE. The 37-leg tenant census put
# 107 objects of type >= 64 into the projectile pool and entered the map ZERO
# times: the sweep is POOL-vs-POOL (both loop registers stride pool slots),
# so a tenant projectile hitting a FIGHTER never transits it. This rig
# supplies the missing half — an OPPOSING PROJECTILE.
#
# THE SHAPE: P1 Pyron runs the 70_pyron_mash chaos body (which is what
# spawns his type 64 satellite); P2 Demitri throws a Chaos Flare every 100
# frames across the same window, so a flare and a satellite occupy the pool
# together. Built on 105_projectile_clash_ctl's proven head-on volley shape
# and 83c's 2P poked-select shape.
#
# BOTH SIDES POKED, early window only (the replay-80 rule):
# POKES="1400:ff8782:11;1450:ff8782:11;1500:ff8782:11;1400:ff8b82:01;1450:ff8b82:01;1500:ff8b82:01"
#
# MEASURED 14z-129 on the pyron stage-6 vertical (a43da974) and its no-thunk
# twin (c4e1057a), both built from the CURRENT manifest, GUARD_DEBUG=1:
#   WITH the thunk    28 probe fires — 14 at map index 0x40 (64, his
#                     satellite) and 14 at 0x04 (Demitri's flare: the sweep
#                     maps BOTH colliding objects) — and END 5020 CLEAN.
#   WITHOUT it        CRASH 3709 vec3 PC 01ab10 ADDR 00ff31b7 — an ODD
#                     address fault at the FIRST index-64 dispatch (f3708).
# That is the f7997 mechanism of 14z-82b reproduced on demand: its write-up
# records "the garbage stream faulted on odd $FF31B5" and A3 = 0xFDC8A;
# this rig faults on odd $FF31B7 with A3 = 0x000FDC8A.
#
# THE INDEX MATTERS AND IS NOT INTERCHANGEABLE. Over-indexing the vanilla
# 64-entry map reads whatever follows it, and the CONSEQUENCE is per-index
# (vsavj opcode view, PRG:0x1A88E):
#     map[64] = 0x4e  pyron satellite   -> LOUD, this crash
#     map[67] = 0x00  pyron             -> the do-nothing default
#     map[68] = 0x12  huitzil grenade   -> SILENT (measured: no crash)
#     map[70] = 0x00  huitzil EX FG     -> the do-nothing default
# A huitzil clash therefore does NOT make a crash control, however real the
# contact is — see tests/replays/hui/96_hui_grenade_clash.rpl. HANDOFF's
# out-of-range doctrine: "no crash" clears a LOUD entry completely and a
# SILENT one not at all.
#
# THE GUARD MUST BE IN -debug MODE. Under GUARD_DEBUG=0 both legs report
# END 5020 and the twin's crash is INVISIBLE: cheap mode installs no
# exception breakpoints, so it cannot see a vec3 (docs/GOTCHAS.md).
